{"id": "EUVD-2026-82084", "enisaUuid": "bc11dd4e-f3e6-3e47-afdd-c0fff51463eb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rxe: Fix UAF in ODP init error-handling path\n\nrxe_odp_mr_init_user() stores &umem_odp->umem in mr->umem before\ncalling rxe_odp_init_pages(). If rxe_odp_init_pages() fails,\nrxe_odp_mr_init_user() releases umem_odp and returns an error.\n\nrxe_reg_user_mr() then unwinds the error through rxe_cleanup(),\nrxe_mr_cleanup(), ib_umem_release(mr->umem). There is an\nIS_ERR_OR_NULL(umem) check at the start of ib_umem_release().\nBut since mr->umem is NOT reset to NULL in the error handling\npath of rxe_odp_mr_init_user(), the check passes and it reads\nalready-freed fields like umem->is_dmabuf, causing UAF.\n\nFix the UAF by clearing mr->umem after releasing the failed\nODP umem so the MR cleanup path does not release it again.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:27", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f1933163327c9f1c8f2a341c6cb551aaf231ff9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cfb448705da3171d44d9cbe7be53ff03284d532", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51f2c8d2c99fc1f452f7113c08a35edcc4bf8732"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vg4x-c29w-66xm", "CVE-2026-90423"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16ce2955-e065-3d14-bdba-82293f2549d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "295b5ce4-0f8b-3b6b-9fd5-cfcb209a0d85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d03fb5c6599e31b90c6b5f65d43d6ccc6b49eb91 <51f2c8d2c99fc1f452f7113c08a35edcc4bf8732"}, {"id": "2dd0e375-acea-3152-a70f-a589fc1b0a52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "87594b8a-544e-36f1-ad2e-8c8415c0144f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d03fb5c6599e31b90c6b5f65d43d6ccc6b49eb91 <4cfb448705da3171d44d9cbe7be53ff03284d532"}, {"id": "acc7fc22-9f33-3ba6-9f45-a3306495dc94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "b2cb446f-3929-3486-b116-ade464430b90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d03fb5c6599e31b90c6b5f65d43d6ccc6b49eb91 <5f1933163327c9f1c8f2a341c6cb551aaf231ff9"}, {"id": "b8327f9b-36f1-31a5-8d6d-afe470aa496f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "e8d080af-be80-3ad6-8525-c0785d4ec7ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1e999f22-1f0d-3c06-9d2b-4c2de8109bb3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}